0011:     """
0012:     Copy the single colored sprite so its bounding-box center lands on the gray marker.
0013: 
0014:     Input structure:
0015:     - A background grid containing one non-gray foreground sprite.
0016:     - Exactly one gray marker pixel sits in an otherwise empty region.
0017:     - The sprite's bounding box has odd height and odd width, so it has a center cell.
0018: 
0019:     Rule:
0020:     - Keep the original sprite unchanged.
0021:     - Extract the full bounding box of the non-gray sprite, treating background cells inside the box as transparent.
0022:     - Paste that sprite box centered on the gray marker, replacing the marker.
0023: 
0024:     Key insight:
0025:     The gray pixel is not a color to preserve; it marks the center of a second copy of the existing sprite.
0026:     """
0027:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0028:     bg = get_bg(g)
0029:     assert bg != Color.GREY
0030: 
0031:     marker_coords = np.argwhere(g == Color.GREY)
0032:     assert len(marker_coords) == 1
0033:     marker_r, marker_c = map(int, marker_coords[0])
0034: 
0035:     sprite_mask = (g != bg) & (g != Color.GREY)
0036:     sprite_components = components_mask(sprite_mask, connectivity=4)
0037:     assert len(sprite_components) == 1
0038: 
0039:     sprite_bbox = bbox(sprite_mask)
